+# Tao window ownership fix
+
+`tao-0.35.3` is the published crate with one change in
+`src/platform_impl/macos/window.rs`. Its original crate SHA-256 is
+`d1c93047acf68669466a34690ac58cca7010bd1b201e1ec86f1fd0a75d3dd4a9`.
+The original licenses remain in the crate directory.
+
+The native constructor uses `alloc` and `initWithContentRect`, which return an
+owned reference. `Retained::retain` adds another reference. The window disables
+release on close, so the extra reference remains after all Rust owners drop.
+The patch uses `Retained::from_raw` to adopt the existing reference.
+
+The native Settings test found 1 Tao window before opening Settings, 21 after
+20 visits, and 41 after 40 visits. Only one WKWebView remained. This is separate
+from the Settings draft, which retains only one snapshot.
+
+References:
+
+- [Tao constructor](https://github.com/tauri-apps/tao/blob/tao-v0.35.3/src/platform_impl/macos/window.rs)
+- [objc2 ownership rules](https://docs.rs/objc2/0.6.4/objc2/rc/struct.Retained.html#method.from_raw)
+
+Before removing this patch, check the replacement constructor and repeat the
+native Settings allocation test. Do not add a compensating native `release`
+call to TinyDash. That would depend on the dependency's reference count.
+
+The patch changes only macOS window creation. It does not change the public
+Tao interface or code for other platforms. It is selected by the root
+`Cargo.toml` patch and recorded in `Cargo.lock`.
